# Windows Performance Troubleshooting Lab

## Overview

In this lab, I used Windows Task Manager and Resource Monitor to investigate a slow Windows 11 workstation.

The goal was to identify what was causing the system slowdown, determine which resources were under the most pressure, and then verify whether closing high-usage applications improved performance.

This lab was completed in a Windows 11 virtual machine running in VMware Fusion.

## Environment

- Windows 11 Enterprise Evaluation
- VMware Fusion
- Task Manager
- Resource Monitor

## Scenario

The workstation was running several applications at the same time, including Microsoft Edge, Outlook, File Explorer, and other Windows applications.

The system started becoming noticeably slower, so I used Task Manager and Resource Monitor to investigate CPU, memory, disk, and network usage.

